      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Burlington was named the first territorial capital of the Iowa Territory when it was organized in 1838.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burlington%2C_Iowa",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Burlington Route, operating from 1848 to 1970, merged into the Burlington Northern Railroad and later became part of today’s BNSF Railway.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
